[469.867425, "o", "> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[469.867472, "o", "### 3.4 Key Observations\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[469.86752, "o", "> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[469.867748, "o", "1. **Smooth Acceleration:** The vehicle accelerates at maximum rate (3.0 m/s²) initially, then smoothly transitions to maintain set speed with minimal overshoot.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[469.867776, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[469.867992, "o", "2. **Effective Following:** When lead vehicle appears, the ACC smoothly transitions to follow mode and maintains appropriate following distance.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n"]
[469.868037, "o", "\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[469.86819, "o", "3. **Safe Operation:** Minimum distance of 19.58 m maintained throughout, well above the 5 m safety threshold.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[469.868238, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[469.868384, "o", "4. **Stable Tracking:** Distance steady-state error of 1.96 m indicates good gap maintenance during follow mode.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[469.86843, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[469.868457, "o", "> ## 4. Conclusions\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n"]
[469.868504, "o", "\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[469.868646, "o", "The implemented ACC system successfully meets all performance targets:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[469.868849, "o", "1. **Speed Control:** Fast response (9.8s rise time) with excellent stability (0.66% overshoot) and accuracy (0.198 m/s SS error).\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n"]
[469.868909, "o", "\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[469.869029, "o", "2. **Distance Control:** Maintains safe following distance with acceptable steady-state error (1.96 m).\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n"]
[469.869088, "o", "\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[469.869213, "o", "3. **Safety:** Large safety margins maintained throughout simulation with minimum distance of 19.58 m.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[469.869262, "o", "> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[469.869515, "o", "The anti-windup mechanism in the PID controller was crucial for preventing overshoot during the initial acceleration phase while still achieving the required rise time.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> EOF\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[469.870892, "o", "\u001b[?2004hroot@5872ab224e04:~# "]
[470.375216, "i", "cat tuning_results.yaml\n"]
[470.375443, "o", "cat tuning_results.yaml\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[470.376216, "o", "# Tuned PID parameters for Adaptive Cruise Control system\r\n# \r\n# Speed Controller Tuning:\r\n#   - Target: rise time <10s, overshoot <5%, SS error <0.5 m/s\r\n#   - Achieved: rise time 9.8s, overshoot 0.66%, SS error 0.198 m/s\r\n#   - Strategy: Moderate kp for adequate response, low ki to prevent windup,\r\n#               high kd to dampen overshoot near setpoint\r\n#\r\n# Distance Controller Tuning:\r\n#   - Target: SS error <2m, min distance >5m\r\n#   - Achieved: SS error 1.96m, min distance 19.58m\r\n#   - Strategy: High kp and ki for tight gap tracking, low kd to avoid\r\n#               oscillation from noisy distance measurements\r\n\r\npid_speed:\r\n  kp: 0.6\r\n  ki: 0.008\r\n  kd: 0.4\r\n\r\npid_distance:\r\n  kp: 4.0\r\n  ki: 0.8\r\n  kd: 0.1\r\n"]
[470.376387, "o", "\u001b[?2004hroot@5872ab224e04:~# "]
[475.644945, "i", "ls -la *.py *.yaml *.csv *.md 2>/dev/null\n"]
[475.645241, "o", "ls -la *.py *.yaml *.csv *.md 2>/dev/null\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
